x,\n$$\n\nwhere $p$ is a constant.\n\nWe can rewrite the given equation as \n\n$$\n{y}^{2}=4(-\\frac{6}{4})x,\n$$\n\nwhich simplifies to\n\n$$\n{y}^{2}=4(-\\frac{3}{2})x.\n$$\n\nIt is now clear that our equation is of the standard type with $p=-\\frac{3}{2}.$ Therefore, our parabola has its vertex at $(0,0).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186097382 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096763 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "9e302810-8b14-5c8c-8bbb-245386a66b7c" :knowledge-point/title "Stating the Vertex of a Horizontal Parabola Given Its Equation in Standard Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bd9ed2af-bce0-5f2e-ac36-d037a91cdb7a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-18,-3)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186377929} {:answer/id #uuid "a5a8f52d-65ba-5029-8566-5a62794a97ed" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-2,3)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186377930} {:answer/id #uuid "407bbf7b-b09d-5986-95c8-e3ee1b82e4e7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(2,3)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186377931} {:answer/id #uuid "27ecc306-ff37-5e60-9788-2d046caccb62" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(2,-3)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186377932} {:answer/id #uuid "aa61bb6d-c2e9-5a7a-a2dc-5b6ed5a04986" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-2,-3)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186377933}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "27ecc306-ff37-5e60-9788-2d046caccb62" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(2,-3)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186377932} :answer-field/id #uuid "f33480cf-d5ae-53d6-9eec-40a595bc5826" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186377928}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "4d8fe4c0-7b61-5a55-898d-20dee3681514" :question/math-academy-id "q-84834" :question/problem "What are the coordinates of the vertex of the parabola $(y+3)^{2}=9(x-2)?$" :question/worked-solution "The standard equation of a left- or right-opening parabola that has its vertex at $(h,k)$ is\n\n$$\n(y-k)^{2}=4p(x-h),\n$$\n\nwhere $p$ is constant.\n\nWe can rewrite the given equation as \n\n$$\n(y+3)^{2}=4(\\frac{9}{4})(x-2).\n$$\n\nIt is now clear that our equation is of the standard type with $p=\\frac{9}{4}.$ \n\nComparing our equation with the standard equation, we can see that we have $h=2$ and $k=-3.$ Therefore, the coordinates of the vertex of the parabola are $(2,-3).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186440816 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096761 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d27b85e4-ddae-5b5f-965a-5dff51b8449b" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Vertex of a Vertical Parabola Given Its Graph"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "336de5f5-e16f-54f1-8315-848c34ce189c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(3,0)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440788} {:answer/id #uuid "74f1e9a2-cd17-53fa-a5d9-ac8793db1138" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-3,0)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440794} {:answer/id #uuid "788a299f-880d-5d7d-914b-db002259928f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(0,-3)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440795} {:answer/id #uuid "e3669f39-573d-5afc-a829-31fc5de4d1e5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(0,0)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440808} {:answer/id #uuid "f3f997ce-031c-5a9d-86ee-ce1e4191b766" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(0,3)" :db/id #edb/ref 175921864408